From d6681fb379364b074ab0ba55cdfd0d65a6a8869a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:37:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] gas: microblaze: test every opcode table entry

The gas tests for MicroBlaze disassemble 32 of the 277 instructions in
opcodes/microblaze-opc.h (26 before the bshift test), and the sleep
pseudo-instruction.  Mask mistakes in the table, where an entry also
matches the encoding of a later entry, show up only when someone
disassembles the later instruction.

The new test covers all 277 instructions, and the sleep, hibernate and
suspend pseudo-instructions, and checks the objdump -d output.  Each
gets one line, except mfs, mfse, mts and mtse, which get one line for
each special register UG984 lists for them.  imm has no line of its own,
because gas does not accept it in source; it appears as the prefix gas
inserts for a large immediate.  The operands put a different value in
each register field (r28, r17, r30), and the immediates set bits at both
ends of their fields.

The expected encodings were not generated from the opcode table.  I
checked every word against the decoder in QEMU 10.2.4
(target/microblaze/insns.decode), which was written independently and
executes the code: QEMU decodes each word to the same instruction with
the same operands in the same fields.  QEMU treats all the wdc forms
as one cache operation, so for those I checked the E, EA, F and T bits
against Figure 141 of the MicroBlaze Processor Reference Guide (UG984,
v2026.1).  sleep, hibernate and suspend are checked against UG984
Table 69, which lists them as assembler pseudo-instructions for mbar 16,
8 and 24.

It also checks that 0x84000400, which objdump printed as pcmpbc until
the previous patch removed it, now prints as .long.

It also has the cases the earlier patches of this series fix or change:
wdc.ext.clear; mbar 9, 17 and 31, with the comments the fourth patch
adds, and mbar 18, 26 and 20 for the rest of that patch's cases; the old
pcmpbc word; and a zero word followed by another instruction.  Against
the tree before the series it fails on exactly those lines and on bslli
and bsrai; with the series it passes.

Tested on microblaze-elf.  gas goes from 332 to 333 expected passes,
with 10 unsupported.  binutils stays at 245 expected passes, 2 expected
failures, 18 untested and 17 unsupported, and ld at 480 expected passes,
15 expected failures, 28 untested and 236 unsupported.  No unexpected
failures.

gas/
	* testsuite/gas/microblaze/insns.exp: New file.
	* testsuite/gas/microblaze/insns.s: New file.
	* testsuite/gas/microblaze/insns.d: New test.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
